WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.770
A patient in hospital is on a drip.

2
00:00:02.820 --> 00:00:07.090
The bag holds 500 cubic
centimetres of salt solution.

3
00:00:07.140 --> 00:00:13.130
The label gives its strength as 9.00
grams of salt per cubic decimetre.

4
00:00:13.180 --> 00:00:16.930
Two different volumes,
and a mass, not an amount.

5
00:00:16.980 --> 00:00:19.810
So how many moles of salt are in the bag?

6
00:00:19.860 --> 00:00:23.510
In this mission, you'll learn what
a concentration really measures,

7
00:00:23.560 --> 00:00:26.450
and how to make up a standard solution.

8
00:00:26.500 --> 00:00:29.850
You'll convert cubic
centimetres to cubic decimetres,

9
00:00:29.900 --> 00:00:34.090
and grams per cubic decimetre
to moles per cubic decimetre.

10
00:00:34.140 --> 00:00:38.270
Your mission: work out how many
moles of salt are in the bag.
